@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Game Submission & Creator Guide";
}

<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>Welcome to BucStop! Here, creators can build and submit their own games for others to enjoy. Below you will find a complete guide that explains the submission requirements, workflow, and how to fork our template repository to create your game.</p>

<hr>

<h2>Game Submission Requirements</h2>

<p>Before submitting a game, ensure it meets the following criteria:</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Game Name:</strong> Must be under 50 characters and free of offensive language.</li>
    <li><strong>Controls:</strong> Must work on both PC and mobile devices.
        <ul>
            <li>Recommended: arrow keys (mobile swipes are automatically mapped to these keys).</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Content:</strong> Must not contain offensive material, including but not limited to:
        <ul>
            <li>Expletives, gore, excessive violence</li>
            <li>Substance use or suggestive content</li>
            <li>Racially insensitive or illegal material</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Technology:</strong> Must be written in JavaScript.</li>
    <li><strong>No Ads:</strong> Your game should be free of advertisements.</li>
    <li><strong>Safety:</strong> Must not include malicious software or harmful scripts.</li>
    <li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Avoid excessive flashing lights or loud sounds.</li>
    <li><strong>Copyright Compliance:</strong> Do not use copyrighted material without permission.</li>
    <li><strong>File Size:</strong> Total game files (including assets) must be ≤ 10MB.</li>
    <li><strong>Canvas Size:</strong> Must be within 640px × 640px.</li>
    <li><strong>User Data:</strong> Only minimal data necessary to save progress can be collected.</li>
    <li><strong>File Organization:</strong> Include all non-JavaScript assets in a dedicated folder.</li>
    <span class="todo">TODO: Go into more detail about the file orginization because it should be set out in template.</span>
</ul>

<hr>

<h2>How Game Submission Works</h2>

<p>Submitting a game to BucStop follows a simple process:</p>
<span class="todo">TODO: Refine instructions based on thorough design of process</span>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Create Your Game:</strong> Fork our official game template repository, which includes a ready-to-use Docker container based on C# MVC.</li>
    <li><strong>Customize and Test:</strong> Modify your container with your JavaScript game and assets. Test on desktop and mobile to ensure it meets all requirements.</li>
    <li><strong>Submit for Review:</strong> Submit your game via our submission form with the repository URL and game details.</li>
    <li><strong>Approval and Deployment:</strong> Once approved, your game will be deployed and listed on BucStop for everyone to play.</li>
</ol>

<hr>

<h2>Step-by-Step Guide for Creators: Forking the Repo</h2>

<p>Follow these steps to start creating your game:</p>

<ol>
    <li><strong>Visit the Template Repository:</strong> Go to our official game template repository (link here).</li>
    <li><strong>Fork the Repository:</strong> Click the <em>Fork</em> button on GitHub to create a personal copy in your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Clone Your Fork Locally:</strong>
        <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/yourusername/template-repo.git</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Open and Modify the Docker Container:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Edit JavaScript, HTML, CSS, and include assets (images, sounds, etc.) in the correct folders.</li>
            <li>Keep the template structure to ensure compatibility with our system.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Run and Test Locally:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Use Docker to build and run your container. Test on both desktop and mobile browsers.</li>
            <li>Verify that your game meets all submission requirements.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Push Changes to Your Fork:</strong>
        <pre><code>git add .
git commit -m "Add my game"
git push origin main</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Submit Your Game:</strong> Fill out the submission form on BucStop and provide the repository URL and game details.</li>
</ol>

<hr>

<h2>Tips for a Successful Submission</h2>

<ul>
    <li>Keep code clean and organized, following the template structure.</li>
    <li>Test thoroughly on both desktop and mobile devices.</li>
    <li>Ensure compliance with content, size, and accessibility requirements.</li>
    <li>Include all non-JavaScript assets in the correct folders for proper container functionality.</li>
</ul>

<p>Following these guidelines ensures a smooth submission process and maximizes the chances your game will be approved and enjoyed by the community!</p>
